Below is the reasoning, the columns that matter, the filtering conditions we will need, and ten exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries (all read‑only, all limited).  
Use them in the given order to drill‑down until we finally learn the two wrestlers in the shortest NXT‑title match that did NOT have a title‑change.

Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• Matches.id            : pick a specific match row.  
• Matches.title_id      : which championship was on the line.  
• Matches.duration      : needed to decide “shortest”.  
• Matches.title_change  : 0 = no change; we must keep only those.  
• Matches.winner_id     : wrestler #1.  
• Matches.loser_id      : wrestler #2.  
• Belts.id              : join‑key to Matches.title_id.  
• Belts.name            : look for “NXT”.  
• Wrestlers.id          : join‑key to winner_id / loser_id.  
• Wrestlers.name        : final wrestler names.  

Filtering conditions we will apply  
1. Belts.name LIKE '%NXT%'                        (any NXT championship)  
2. Matches.title_change = 0                       (exclude title changes)  
3. Matches.duration <> ''                         (ignore blank duration)  
4. Among those rows, choose the smallest duration (shortest match).  

Ten step‑by‑step queries
--------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1.  List every belt; verify which names contain “NXT”.
SELECT DISTINCT id, name
FROM Belts
ORDER BY name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  Show the belt‑ids that actually contain the word “NXT”.
SELECT id AS nxt_belt_id, name
FROM Belts
WHERE name LIKE '%NXT%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Find all Matches that involved one of those NXT belts.
SELECT DISTINCT m.id, m.title_id, m.duration, m.title_change
FROM Matches AS m
WHERE m.title_id IN (SELECT id FROM Belts WHERE name LIKE '%NXT%')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4.  Same as #3 but keep ONLY matches with a recorded duration.
SELECT DISTINCT m.id, m.duration
FROM Matches AS m
WHERE m.title_id IN (SELECT id FROM Belts WHERE name LIKE '%NXT%')
  AND m.duration <> ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5.  Now also exclude title changes (title_change = 0).
SELECT DISTINCT m.id, m.duration
FROM Matches AS m
WHERE m.title_id IN (SELECT id FROM Belts WHERE name LIKE '%NXT%')
  AND m.duration <> ''
  AND m.title_change = 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6.  Order the remaining NXT matches by duration length
--     (first by string length, then alphabetically) to see which is shortest.
SELECT m.id, m.duration
FROM Matches AS m
WHERE m.title_id IN (SELECT id FROM Belts WHERE name LIKE '%NXT%')
  AND m.duration <> ''
  AND m.title_change = 0
ORDER BY LENGTH(m.duration), m.duration
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7.  Grab ONLY the very shortest one (1 row).
SELECT m.id AS shortest_match_id, m.duration
FROM Matches AS m
WHERE m.title_id IN (SELECT id FROM Belts WHERE name LIKE '%NXT%')
  AND m.duration <> ''
  AND m.title_change = 0
ORDER BY LENGTH(m.duration), m.duration
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 8.  Using the id we just discovered, pull the winner & loser wrestler‑ids.
SELECT m.id, m.winner_id, m.loser_id
FROM Matches AS m
WHERE m.id = (
      SELECT m2.id
      FROM Matches AS m2
      WHERE m2.title_id IN (SELECT id FROM Belts WHERE name LIKE '%NXT%')
        AND m2.duration <> ''
        AND m2.title_change = 0
      ORDER BY LENGTH(m2.duration), m2.duration
      LIMIT 1
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9.  Translate those two wrestler‑ids into names.
SELECT w.id, w.name
FROM Wrestlers AS w
WHERE w.id IN (
     SELECT m.winner_id FROM Matches m
     WHERE m.id = (
          SELECT m2.id
          FROM Matches AS m2
          WHERE m2.title_id IN (SELECT id FROM Belts WHERE name LIKE '%NXT%')
            AND m2.duration <> ''
            AND m2.title_change = 0
          ORDER BY LENGTH(m2.duration), m2.duration
          LIMIT 1
     )
     UNION
     SELECT m.loser_id FROM Matches m
     WHERE m.id = (
          SELECT m2.id
          FROM Matches AS m2
          WHERE m2.title_id IN (SELECT id FROM Belts WHERE name LIKE '%NXT%')
            AND m2.duration <> ''
            AND m2.title_change = 0
          ORDER BY LENGTH(m2.duration), m2.duration
          LIMIT 1
     )
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL single‑shot query:
--     names of the two wrestlers in the shortest NXT title match (no title change).
SELECT w1.name  AS wrestler_1,
       w2.name  AS wrestler_2
FROM Matches   AS m
JOIN Belts     AS b  ON b.id = m.title_id
JOIN Wrestlers AS w1 ON w1.id = m.winner_id
JOIN Wrestlers AS w2 ON w2.id = m.loser_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.duration <> ''
  AND m.title_change = 0
ORDER BY LENGTH(m.duration), m.duration
LIMIT 1;
```

